# cs2gs ilverify allow-unsafe marker (gsharp issue #1933 / #1985).
#
# These types perform low-level binary/crypto parsing with `stackalloc`
# (Span<byte> over a localloc buffer). `localloc` is inherently unverifiable
# IL — the C# compiler emits the exact same unverifiable instruction for the
# same source — so ilverify legitimately reports "Unverifiable" for their
# methods. This is expected-unverifiable, not a gsc emit bug. Scope the
# allowance to just these fixture types so a genuine unsafe-IL regression
# elsewhere in the app still gates.
Oahu.Decrypt.Mpeg4.Boxes.Stz2Box
Oahu.Decrypt.Mpeg4.ID3.APICFrame
Oahu.Decrypt.Mpeg4.ID3.FrameHeader
Oahu.Decrypt.Mpeg4.ID3.Header
Oahu.Decrypt.Mpeg4.ID3.Id3Header
Oahu.Decrypt.Mpeg4.ID3.TXXXFrame
Oahu.Decrypt.Mpeg4.Util.AesCtr
Oahu.Decrypt.Mpeg4.Util.HelperExtensions
